  "term": "two-way analysis of variance",
  "definition": "Two-way analysis of variance is an ANOVA-based statistical method used to analyze experimental data. The packet indicates that, when it is implemented in software, the reported p-values can depend on the options chosen, so results may vary and may be less reliable in some small or mixed-effects analyses.",
